Sigh.  One more time for everyone who doesn't understand.

THIS _IS_ THE STANDARDLY DISTRIBUTED VERSION!

The point is that it works differently on different computers.  Get it??  You
don't have to make any changes at all.  The standard version compiled on an
Amiga computer will give you three windows and pulldown menus.  If you compile
it on different computers you won't get that OR the coding that produces it
will be entirely different.  The standard release has sections of code that
only apply to specific computers.

The above problem with the -127 lower limit is again NOT a modification to the
code.  It is a result of the fact that while an 8 bit machine can only have
256 permutations in a schar aa 16 bit machine could have alot more (and no, I'm
not going to calculate how much).  The same code produces different results
depending on the hardware.
